WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.958 --> 00:00:02.268
To empower girls,

00:00:02.292 --> 00:00:03.934
you need to educate them.

00:00:03.958 --> 00:00:05.518
That was my dream.

00:00:05.542 --> 00:00:07.143
And so I built a school,

00:00:07.167 --> 00:00:10.059
and in the process,
I learned something much bigger.

00:00:10.083 --> 00:00:13.042
When you empower a girl,
you transform a community.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:15.750
School is just a start.

00:00:17.042 --> 00:00:18.476
I grew up in rural Kenya

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:21.226
in a small village called Enoosaen.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:22.893
I was the first of eight children,

00:00:22.917 --> 00:00:28.059
and I spent my childhood
helping my mother cook, clean, farm

00:00:28.083 --> 00:00:30.018
and take care of my siblings.

00:00:30.042 --> 00:00:31.934
Like other Maasai girls,

00:00:31.958 --> 00:00:35.500
I was engaged from
a very young age to be married.

00:00:36.375 --> 00:00:38.059
But as I reached puberty,

00:00:38.083 --> 00:00:40.917
I underwent female genital mutilation,

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.292
known as FGM.

00:00:44.208 --> 00:00:49.417
This picture shows some of the tools
that are used to perform FGM on girls.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.518
FGM was supposed to mark
the end of my childhood

00:00:54.542 --> 00:00:57.500
and, by extension, my education.

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:02.351
But I negotiated with my father
in order to stay in school --

00:01:02.375 --> 00:01:04.292
even after going through FGM.

00:01:05.958 --> 00:01:08.625
Years later I went to university.

00:01:09.625 --> 00:01:13.934
And in order to get
my community's support,

00:01:13.958 --> 00:01:18.083
I promised to come back one day
to repay that support.

00:01:18.875 --> 00:01:22.226
But years later,
when I went back to my village,

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:23.792
not much had changed.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:27.184
Girls were still going through FGM,

00:01:27.208 --> 00:01:28.934
still leaving school,

00:01:28.958 --> 00:01:32.393
still getting married
to men older than their fathers

00:01:32.417 --> 00:01:36.708
and still having children
when they're teenagers.

00:01:37.375 --> 00:01:41.143
I did not want to see
any more girls go through that.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:45.625
That's when I knew what I needed to do
to give back to my community.

00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:50.559
I built a school just for girls

00:01:50.583 --> 00:01:54.333
so that they can be free from FGM
and early marriage.

00:01:55.083 --> 00:01:56.643
At my first enrollment --

00:01:56.667 --> 00:02:00.833
(Applause and cheers)

00:02:03.292 --> 00:02:05.059
At my first enrollment,

00:02:05.083 --> 00:02:07.333
I had hoped for 10 girls.

00:02:07.958 --> 00:02:09.434
100 came.

00:02:09.458 --> 00:02:11.351
(Cheers and applause)

00:02:11.375 --> 00:02:15.268
I started to realize
just how big this dream was,

00:02:15.292 --> 00:02:19.476
and soon I learned that my school
could be the foundation --

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.684
but it wasn't going to be enough.

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:25.684
So that first year,
I enrolled these 30 girls.

00:02:25.708 --> 00:02:28.309
Some had been abused, others were orphans,

00:02:28.333 --> 00:02:30.893
and some came from families
that are very traditional,

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:32.792
that had never sent any girl to school.

00:02:33.625 --> 00:02:34.917
So school started.

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:38.059
Though the girls
seemed excited to be there,

00:02:38.083 --> 00:02:40.833
they were having difficulty staying awake.

00:02:41.917 --> 00:02:43.309
What was going on?

00:02:43.333 --> 00:02:45.184
They had a teacher, they had books,

00:02:45.208 --> 00:02:47.851
there was a new classroom on the way,

00:02:47.875 --> 00:02:49.143
but ...

00:02:49.167 --> 00:02:53.083
They were determined to be there,
but they had no energy.

00:02:53.708 --> 00:02:55.375
Then I realized they were hungry,

00:02:56.458 --> 00:02:59.250
so I quickly found a cook and food.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.684
Soon thereafter, I learned
that a classroom was not enough.

00:03:03.708 --> 00:03:05.958
I needed a boarding school.

00:03:06.542 --> 00:03:10.768
Not only were the girls tired
and hungry from chores

00:03:10.792 --> 00:03:13.726
and long walks to school and back home,

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:15.643
they were also not safe.

00:03:15.667 --> 00:03:17.393
It's a sad truth,

00:03:17.417 --> 00:03:21.434
but girls are often assaulted,
raped and even kidnapped

00:03:21.458 --> 00:03:22.708
on their way to school.

00:03:23.917 --> 00:03:27.018
So before a girl
could learn math or history,

00:03:27.042 --> 00:03:28.934
she needed to feel safe,

00:03:28.958 --> 00:03:32.083
she needed to be rested
and be well-nourished.

00:03:32.958 --> 00:03:35.434
So let me tell you about some of my girls.

00:03:35.458 --> 00:03:37.018
This is Faith.

00:03:37.042 --> 00:03:41.143
Faith comes from a very traditional
family in the community.

00:03:41.167 --> 00:03:45.643
Her older sister had already
gone through FGM and already married,

00:03:45.667 --> 00:03:47.768
but Faith was so determined.

00:03:47.792 --> 00:03:49.309
She really loved learning,

00:03:49.333 --> 00:03:53.059
and she wanted to come to my school
when she heard about it.

00:03:53.083 --> 00:03:55.726
So she asked her father, her mother --

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:58.059
anyone to bring her to my school.

00:03:58.083 --> 00:03:59.875
They all refused.

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:03.101
Faith did something very brave.

00:04:03.125 --> 00:04:06.393
She stole an egg from her mother's house,

00:04:06.417 --> 00:04:07.684
went to the market,

00:04:07.708 --> 00:04:10.184
sold the egg and bought a single pencil.

00:04:10.208 --> 00:04:12.018
Then she walked five miles,

00:04:12.042 --> 00:04:14.375
clenching that pencil, trying to enroll.

00:04:15.625 --> 00:04:16.892
She arrived --

00:04:16.916 --> 00:04:19.059
(Applause)

00:04:19.083 --> 00:04:22.184
She arrived tired and hungry,

00:04:22.208 --> 00:04:23.684
but determined.

00:04:23.708 --> 00:04:27.768
I listened to her story,
and we enrolled her in my school.

00:04:27.792 --> 00:04:30.833
But getting into my school
was only just the start.

00:04:31.875 --> 00:04:33.976
Faith needed food, she needed medicine,

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:35.292
she needed counseling --

00:04:36.292 --> 00:04:37.625
all of which we provided.

00:04:38.375 --> 00:04:41.833
And she also met adults
who already believed in her.

00:04:42.833 --> 00:04:45.226
Supported by this community,

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:46.625
Faith was ready to learn.

00:04:47.333 --> 00:04:48.851
This is Faith.

00:04:48.875 --> 00:04:51.059
Six months of schooling,

00:04:51.083 --> 00:04:55.976
now she's a happy sixth grader
who dreams of becoming a pilot someday,

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.768
and her family now supports her,

00:04:58.792 --> 00:05:00.309
and best of all,

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:03.351
her younger sisters
will follow in her footsteps.

00:05:03.375 --> 00:05:07.500
(Applause)

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:16.184
Child marriage is expected to cost
the global economy trillions of dollars

00:05:16.208 --> 00:05:18.083
over the next 15 years.

00:05:18.708 --> 00:05:20.809
We can talk numbers,

00:05:20.833 --> 00:05:22.393
but in a real lifetime,

00:05:22.417 --> 00:05:28.143
what child marriage will cost my village
is the doctor, the teacher,

00:05:28.167 --> 00:05:29.476
the entrepreneur,

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:32.583
the true partner our men
will need in the future ...

00:05:33.417 --> 00:05:37.708
real ways women can help us
lift out of poverty.

00:05:39.208 --> 00:05:42.393
So I came to realize once again,

00:05:42.417 --> 00:05:45.476
as I did when I needed help
to go to university,

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:48.934
that while I could dream or have a dream,

00:05:48.958 --> 00:05:52.958
I could not make it come true
all by myself.

00:05:53.875 --> 00:05:58.518
So I went back to the elders
who helped me more than a decade ago.

00:05:58.542 --> 00:06:02.833
I needed their support once again
if I was going to be successful.

00:06:03.708 --> 00:06:08.309
So I formed a community board
with religious leaders, parents

00:06:08.333 --> 00:06:11.559
and some teachers from other schools.

00:06:11.583 --> 00:06:15.434
I needed allies in the government
and in the community

00:06:15.458 --> 00:06:18.059
to help advance my goal.

00:06:18.083 --> 00:06:20.726
I needed especially
the support of the chief

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:24.083
to help me enforce
the no-FGM policy in my school.

00:06:24.833 --> 00:06:27.476
At first he was resistant,

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:28.768
but I persisted --

00:06:28.792 --> 00:06:30.059
(Laughter)

00:06:30.083 --> 00:06:32.934
and now he's our greatest ally.

00:06:32.958 --> 00:06:38.309
(Applause)

00:06:38.333 --> 00:06:40.542
I also needed the fathers.

00:06:41.958 --> 00:06:44.351
That brings me to Linet.

00:06:44.375 --> 00:06:49.059
Linet's father, Momposhi,
did not believe in the education of girls.

00:06:49.083 --> 00:06:52.101
In fact, he himself never went to school.

00:06:52.125 --> 00:06:55.726
But Linet's mother believed in Linet
and brought her to enroll in my school,

00:06:55.750 --> 00:06:58.018
and I knew she belonged with us.

00:06:58.042 --> 00:07:03.333
I just had to find a way
to get Momposhi to believe in Linet, too.

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:08.226
So I used the pretense
of revealing Linet's grade

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:11.101
to get Momposhi to come.

00:07:11.125 --> 00:07:15.958
He came, and he started noticing
his daughter being promising as a student.

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:22.143
With each visit, he built
a strong relationship with his daughter --

00:07:22.167 --> 00:07:24.601
noticing not just her grades

00:07:24.625 --> 00:07:28.208
but also accepting her
as someone with full potential.

00:07:29.917 --> 00:07:33.184
So when Linet was accepted
in one of the top national high schools

00:07:33.208 --> 00:07:34.893
after eighth grade,

00:07:34.917 --> 00:07:37.601
Momposhi was bursting with pride

00:07:37.625 --> 00:07:38.934
and went around the village

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:42.684
telling everyone how proud
and how smart his daughter was.

00:07:42.708 --> 00:07:43.851
(Laughter)

00:07:43.875 --> 00:07:45.143
Can you imagine?

00:07:45.167 --> 00:07:47.809
He brought Linet
to the new school himself.

00:07:47.833 --> 00:07:51.625
It was the first time either of them
had ever been to Nairobi.

00:07:52.458 --> 00:07:56.601
Today Linet is studying
at university in Australia --

00:07:56.625 --> 00:08:01.851
(Applause and cheers)

00:08:01.875 --> 00:08:05.333
and Momposhi is our greatest
advocate in the community.

00:08:06.375 --> 00:08:08.726
I also brought mothers to the table,

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:10.268
including my own.

00:08:10.292 --> 00:08:12.893
That's my mother
in one of our training programs.

00:08:12.917 --> 00:08:16.333
And our mothers are involved
in the education of their own children.

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:19.684
I also brought grandmothers into the mix.

00:08:19.708 --> 00:08:20.809
(Laughter)

00:08:20.833 --> 00:08:23.934
In my community, grandmothers
are the proud keepers

00:08:23.958 --> 00:08:26.059
of our stories and cultures,

00:08:26.083 --> 00:08:30.708
and I wanted my girls to learn
and embrace our rich Maasai culture.

00:08:31.333 --> 00:08:34.101
Today, grandmothers
do story time with the girls,

00:08:34.125 --> 00:08:37.832
and it's a beautiful way
our community remains connected.

00:08:39.792 --> 00:08:41.042
I also ...

00:08:41.917 --> 00:08:43.433
started working with the boys!

00:08:43.457 --> 00:08:44.559
(Laughter)

00:08:44.583 --> 00:08:45.934
What would happen

00:08:45.958 --> 00:08:50.476
if the boys grew up with the same
mindset as their fathers before them?

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:53.000
I'll tell you, not much will change.

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:58.684
So I enlisted support from an organization
called I'm Worth Defending:

00:08:58.708 --> 00:09:03.101
a group of young, progressive leaders
led by Alfred and George.

00:09:03.125 --> 00:09:06.893
Together we created
a training program for boys and girls

00:09:06.917 --> 00:09:09.059
who could not attend my school,

00:09:09.083 --> 00:09:13.559
sharing vital information
about gender equality,

00:09:13.583 --> 00:09:15.542
health and human rights.

00:09:16.208 --> 00:09:21.851
Today we have reached
over 10,000 boys and girls and counting.

00:09:21.875 --> 00:09:25.875
(Applause)

00:09:28.917 --> 00:09:33.601
It turns out it truly does take a village
to make this kind of a dream come true.

00:09:33.625 --> 00:09:34.976
(Laughter)

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:36.684
That's what you're seeing today,

00:09:36.708 --> 00:09:41.393
where nearly 400 girls
have not gone through FGM

00:09:41.417 --> 00:09:42.893
in my village,

00:09:42.917 --> 00:09:47.500
in a region where nearly 80 percent
of women have been cut.

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:51.518
Believe me, these girls,

00:09:51.542 --> 00:09:53.768
they are sharing their experiences

00:09:53.792 --> 00:09:57.851
with their sisters,
their cousins and their friends.

00:09:57.875 --> 00:10:00.250
They're so interested.

00:10:01.042 --> 00:10:03.684
Over time, this is becoming the new normal

00:10:03.708 --> 00:10:07.309
and it's being embraced
by the same, same community --

00:10:07.333 --> 00:10:08.583
my community.

00:10:09.792 --> 00:10:13.708
So what does transforming
communities mean to Kenya?

00:10:15.167 --> 00:10:18.351
President Obama visited Kenya in 2015,

00:10:18.375 --> 00:10:22.018
and he met with representatives
from organizations

00:10:22.042 --> 00:10:25.042
trying to help improve communities.

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:27.309
Guess what?

00:10:27.333 --> 00:10:28.643
He met Linet!

00:10:28.667 --> 00:10:30.351
(Laughter)

00:10:30.375 --> 00:10:33.708
(Applause)

00:10:37.917 --> 00:10:40.184
Together they talked about a Kenya

00:10:40.208 --> 00:10:44.018
where all girls
have the same opportunities,

00:10:44.042 --> 00:10:46.268
where Linet is a leader

00:10:46.292 --> 00:10:49.351
and where communities
like Enoosaen are thriving

00:10:49.375 --> 00:10:50.726
because its members --

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:53.375
all its members -- have opportunities.

00:10:53.958 --> 00:10:57.934
Helping the communities see
that each daughter is a treasure,

00:10:57.958 --> 00:11:00.226
every sister is full of potential,

00:11:00.250 --> 00:11:04.333
and helping every single girl
see that value in herself.

00:11:04.917 --> 00:11:08.458
There is no limit
to what that future will cost.

00:11:09.833 --> 00:11:14.476
Not every girl who comes
to my school will be a PhD,

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:19.601
but every single one of them
will achieve her full potential

00:11:19.625 --> 00:11:22.726
and will become an advocate
for her children

00:11:22.750 --> 00:11:25.958
and her grandchildren for years to come.

00:11:26.667 --> 00:11:30.518
Today my dreams are informed
by what I learned from them

00:11:30.542 --> 00:11:32.019
and what I've learned from you.

00:11:32.625 --> 00:11:36.417
My journey led me
out of Enoosaen and back again.

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:38.518
And in the process,

00:11:38.542 --> 00:11:40.292
I was embraced by the world,

00:11:41.042 --> 00:11:43.309
and you have become my village.

00:11:43.333 --> 00:11:45.726
So I make a new promise to you,

00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:49.309
my elders, my sisters and my friends,

00:11:49.333 --> 00:11:53.351
that I am going to keep
dreaming and keep going

00:11:53.375 --> 00:11:57.559
until girls like Linet and Faith
achieve their dreams

00:11:57.583 --> 00:11:59.476
and I see mine:

00:11:59.500 --> 00:12:04.726
that all communities
give every single woman

00:12:04.750 --> 00:12:06.393
and every single girl

00:12:06.417 --> 00:12:08.559
their dreams come true.

00:12:08.583 --> 00:12:09.851
Thank you.

00:12:09.875 --> 00:12:12.167
(Applause and cheers)

00:12:14.083 --> 00:12:16.143
Thank you, thank you.

00:12:16.167 --> 00:12:17.875
(Applause and cheers)

